## Epic 0: Mostly Faithful Baseline - Starting Area
Baby step to validate port with relaxed matching.
- Port/verify Samus physics, collision, door transitions, basic enemies in Crateria/starting room using existing `sm_a*.c`, `sm_80.c` etc. (pretty close is acceptable)
- Load save states from `custom_integrations/SuperMetroid-Snes/`.
- Add automated tests: physics sim, collision cases. Screenshot regression optional.
- Document function coverage (`grep -r "TODO\|UNIMPLEMENTED"`).
- TODO: strict 100% frame-by-frame verification for all edge cases (lower priority).
- Implement `make test` harness tied to Python tools.
- Achieve solid gameplay match for 1-2 rooms.

## Epic 1: Extract & Mod Physics
Foundation for modding.
- Refactor all Samus physics (subpixel, accel, jump tables, momentum, grapple, shinespark, etc.) into `PhysicsParams` struct with original defaults.
- Add file-based config + live reload.
- Expose to debug menu/editor for real-time tweaking (gravity, speed, etc.).
- [x] Support multiple independent Samus instances.
- [x] Unit tests for speedrun tech (walljumps, mock inputs).
- [x] Add 2nd player controls.

## Epic 2: Full Logic Port & Hybrid Dispatcher
Complete reverse engineering.
- Systematically port remaining banks (`sm_*.c` files) referencing external decomp and `../sm/`.
- Build hybrid dispatcher in `sm_cpu_infra.c`: C func if available, else emulate original opcode/assembly chunk.
- One bank per iteration (enemies, bosses, items, menu, etc.).
- Comprehensive per-module tests.
- Gradually reduce reliance on full emulation.

## Epic 3: Entity & Enemy Framework
Make enemies/players fully editable.
- Data-driven enemy defs (sprites, hitboxes, AI states, behaviors as tables or scripts).
- Refactor update/init routines to use data.
- Editor/tools for adding new enemies, modifying stats/AI.
- Multi-Samus support (different abilities per player).
- Hooks for custom behaviors without touching core code.

## Epic 4: Level/World Canvas & Editor
"Vibe edit" everything.
- Decouple levels from ROM; load from data files or editor.
- In-game or external canvas/editor (build on Super Metroid editor + ImGui overlay) for tiles, entities, triggers, doors.
- Support entirely new worlds/maps for same Samus.
- Integration with `navigation/` graph tools and `platformer_common`.
- Export to ROM-hack format or standalone.

## Epic 5: Multiplayer, Stories & Game Modes
- Local split-screen / co-op / vs.
- Basic netcode for online multiplayer.
- Data-driven cutscenes/stories for new campaigns.
- Dedicated battle arena mode with custom rules/enemies.
